# SecondChance web app — environment
#
# Every variable here is optional. With none of them set the app runs against
# the City of Austin's public open-data feeds anonymously, which is enough for
# development and for a low-traffic deployment.
#
# There are no NEXT_PUBLIC_ variables. Austin is contacted server-side only, so
# nothing in this file may be given that prefix: a NEXT_PUBLIC_ token is
# readable by anyone who opens devtools.

# Socrata application token. Optional, and it is not a credential in the usual
# sense: it does not grant access to anything, it just gives this app its own
# throttling pool instead of sharing the anonymous one. Worth setting before
# the site takes real traffic. Sent as the X-App-Token header, server-side.
#
#   https://dev.socrata.com/docs/app-tokens.html
SOCRATA_APP_TOKEN=

# Dataset overrides. The ids below are the defaults compiled into
# src/lib/austin/datasets.ts and are only worth setting if Austin republishes a
# feed under a new id and you need to repoint it without a deploy.
#
# The two current feeds are the ShelterBuddy era, 5 May 2025 onward, refreshed
# hourly. They are what the site reads.
# AUSTIN_CURRENT_INTAKES_ID=pyqf-r2dc
# AUSTIN_CURRENT_OUTCOMES_ID=gsvs-ypi7
#
# The two archive feeds are frozen at the May 2025 cutover and are used by the
# offline study only. They do not share an animal-id namespace with the current
# feeds and must never be concatenated with them.
# AUSTIN_ARCHIVE_INTAKES_ID=wter-evkm
# AUSTIN_ARCHIVE_OUTCOMES_ID=9t4d-g238

# Set to 1 to run tests/live-austin.test.ts, which fetches the real feeds and
# checks the episode join against an independent anti-join. Skipped by default
# so the suite stays offline and fast.
# AUSTIN_LIVE_TESTS=1
